# Git workflow

After completing implementation work (features, fixes, refactors):

1. Commit all relevant changes with a concise message focused on **why**.
2. Push to `origin` on the current branch immediately — do **not** ask for permission.
3. Do not push secrets (`.env`, credentials). Warn if those are staged.
4. Never force-push to `main`/`master` unless explicitly requested.

## After every push to `main`

1. **Vercel** — auto-deploys the web app from Git; no manual `vercel --prod` needed.
2. **APK** — GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/build-apk.yml`) builds and publishes
   `marasim-prod-latest.apk` to the [apk-latest release](https://github.com/KWMIOK/marasim/releases/tag/apk-latest).
3. **Local APK** — when working in this repo on a machine with Android SDK/Java, also run
   `npm run cap:apk:prod` after pushing so
   `android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk` is ready for USB install.

Skip commit/push only when the user explicitly says not to, or when there are zero file changes.
